  "notes": "chi(|H>^6) <= 7 is the six-copy value behind the standard 2^{0.47n} figure (log_2(7)/6 = 0.468). This entry replaces one that listed rank 6 here and attributed it to Bravyi and Gosset (arXiv:1601.07601); that paper bounds the approximate stabilizer rank, not the exact one, and a rank 6 at six copies would give exponent 0.431, below the 0.463 that Qassim, Pashayan and Gosset (arXiv:2106.07740) name as the best previously known, so no such value was in the literature. Witness found here by the package's annealer (search_decomposition.py, target qubit_real, seed 3, starting rank 7) and verified in exact arithmetic; two further runs starting at rank 6 (seeds 1 and 2) both terminated at residual 0.101, consistent with a plateau rather than a missed solution."
